<title>USA: Zulauf picks undervalued stocks -Barron's.</title>
<headline>Zulauf picks undervalued stocks -Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Felix Zulauf, head of Zulauf Asset Management in Zug, Switzerland, gave a list of stocks he believes to be undervalued in the Monday edition of Barron's.</p>
<p>Zulauf was one of four top money managers interviewed in Barron's, the financial weekly.</p>
<p>He listed the following shares:</p>
<p>Travelers Group Inc</p>
<p>Internationale Nederlanden Groep NV</p>
<p>Telefon AB L.M. Ericsson</p>
<p>Oy Nokia AB</p>
<p>Elf Aquitaine  </p>
<p>Saga Petroleum A/S</p>
<p>Telecom Italia SpA</p>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG</p>
<p>Philips Electronics Corp</p>
<p>Credit National  </p>
<p>Asturiana de Zinc SA</p>
<p>and Jelfa SA.  </p>
<p>((Reuters News Desk))</p>
</text>
